
### A home with no board is unchanged: no agenda line, nothing else moved
$ bin/fm-board.sh wake-line
<no output>
$ bin/fm-wake-drain.sh   # no board, empty queue


### The agenda records the goal, its check, its state, and the next bounded action
$ bin/fm-board.sh next
1	restore weekly chart freshness	rerun the chart build with the new window	served range equals this week
$ bin/fm-board.sh wake-line
BOARD NEXT: item 1 "restore weekly chart freshness" - next: rerun the chart build with the new window | done when: served range equals this week | run it this turn unless this wake carries captain-class content

### A busy main drain puts the agenda line ahead of its wake rows
$ bin/fm-wake-drain.sh   # one queued wake
BOARD NEXT: item 1 "restore weekly chart freshness" - next: rerun the chart build with the new window | done when: served range equals this week | run it this turn unless this wake carries captain-class content
1794585372	1	signal	task-a.status	signal: task-a
  stderr: WAKE_ACK_REQUIRED: after handling completes run bin/fm-wake-drain.sh --ack-through 1 --recovery-generation 511147.1794585372.L5NJsA

### An hour with an unblocked item and no advance wakes firstmate with the item to drive
$ bin/fm-board-audit.sh check   # +61m, unchanged board
board audit: no item advanced in 61m while item 1 is unblocked -> drive item 1 "restore weekly chart freshness": rerun the chart build with the new window
$ bin/fm-board-audit.sh check   # +62m, same state
<silent: one reminder per cadence>

### The armed check shim is what the watcher polls, and it carries the same line
$ bin/fm-board-audit.sh arm
armed: state/board-audit.check.sh
$ state/board-audit.check.sh   # +92m, past the 30m reminder cadence
board audit: no item advanced in 92m while item 1 is unblocked -> drive item 1 "restore weekly chart freshness": rerun the chart build with the new window
record: 1794590892
idle:1:restore weekly chart freshness

### Driving the item clears the alarm instead of reporting the same state again
$ bin/fm-board.sh advance 1 "build rerun, served range equals this week" --next "watch the next scheduled build"
$ bin/fm-board-audit.sh check   # +93m, after the advance
<silent>
$ bin/fm-board.sh next
1	restore weekly chart freshness	watch the next scheduled build	served range equals this week

### A blocker is raised to the captain at most twice, then it is a defect
$ bin/fm-board.sh block 2 "refund needs captain approval" --captain money
$ bin/fm-board.sh escalate 2   # raising 1
escalation 1 of 2 for item 2
  exit=0
$ bin/fm-board.sh escalate 2   # raising 2
escalation 2 of 2 for item 2: this is the last one - solve it or leave it blocked and drive the next item
  exit=0
$ bin/fm-board.sh escalate 2   # raising 3
fm-board: item 2 blocker was already raised 2 times; a third raising is a defect - leave it blocked and drive the next item
  exit=5
$ bin/fm-board.sh next   # the blocked item no longer stops the agenda
1	restore weekly chart freshness	watch the next scheduled build	served range equals this week

### The same needs-decision key raised again in timestamp-first and indented lines is a defect
$ bin/fm-board-audit.sh check   # +94m
board audit: no item advanced in 94m while item 1 is unblocked; needs-decision lane-a/dns raised x2 unanswered (answer it or hold it, then move on) -> drive item 1 "restore weekly chart freshness": watch the next scheduled build

### Disarming leaves the home without the check shim or its record
disarmed: state/board-audit.check.sh
